static const char chunk27[]=R"NATIVE_DATA(":"married 在这里表示“已婚的”。"},{"id":"word9","kind":"meaning","phase":"理解词义","wordId":"u1b-w10","title":"single 在这里是什么意思？","text":"He is single and lives with a friend.","options":["单身的","兴趣","姓"],"answer":0,"why":"single 在这里表示“单身的”。"},{"id":"read0","kind":"read","phase":"阅读理解","title":"读懂这段信息","text":"Ben is Mei’s colleague. He is usually quiet at work, but he is friendly and helpful. He helps new colleagues find the right room. His cousin Leo is tall and likes talking to people. Leo is married. Ben is single and lives with a friend. Their neighbour Rosa works in a busy café. She is kind to the people who visit. Ben and Rosa study English together on Tuesday evenings. A quiet person can still be friendly; one adjective does not tell you everything about a person.","q":"Ben 安静，是否说明他不友好？","options":["是，quiet 就是不友好","不是，他也友好且乐于助人","文章没有描述他的性格"],"answer":1,"why":"quiet 描述话多话少，friendly 描述待人的方式，两者可以同时成立。"},{"id":"read1","kind":"read","phase":"阅读理解","title":"读懂这段信息","text":"Ben is Mei’s colleague. He is usually quiet at work, but he is friendly and helpful. He helps new colleagues find the right room. His cousin Leo is tall and likes talking to people. Leo is married. Ben is single and lives with a friend. Their neighbour Rosa works in a busy café. She is kind to the people who visit. Ben and Rosa study English together on Tuesday evenings. A quiet person can still be friendly; one adjective does not tell you everything about a person.","q":"谁已经结婚？","options":["Ben","Rosa","Leo"],"answer":2,"why":"Leo is married；Ben is single。注意人名与状态的对应。"},{"id":"read2","kind":"read","phase":"阅读理解","title":"读懂这段信息","text":"Ben is Mei’s colleague. He is usually quiet at work, but he is friendly and helpful. He helps new colleagues find the right room. His cousin Leo is tall and likes talking to people. Leo is married. Ben is single and lives with a friend. Their neighbour Rosa works in a busy café. She is kind to the people who visit. Ben and Rosa study English together on Tuesday evenings. A quiet person can still be friendly; one adjective does not tell you everything about a person.","q":"Ben 和 Rosa 什么时候一起学英语？","options":["周二晚上","每天上午","周日中午"],"answer":0,"why":"together 表明一起，on Tuesday evenings 给出时间。"},{"id":"listen0","kind":"listen","phase":"听力理解","title":"先听，再选择","text":"A: Is your new colleague friendly? B: Yes, and she is very helpful. A: Is she quiet? B: Not really. She likes talking to people.","q":"新同事是什么样的人？","options":["友好并乐于助人","不喜欢交谈","总是很安静"],"answer":0,"why":"回答先肯定 friendly 和 helpful，再否定 quiet。"},{"id":"listen1","kind":"listen","phase":"听力理解","title":"先听，再选择","text":"A: Are you busy on Tuesday evening? B: Yes. My cousin and I study English together. I am free on Wednesday.","q":"对方哪天有空？","options":["星期二","星期三","两天都没空"],"answer":1,"why":"周二一起学英语，周三有空；需要听完转折后的安排。"},{"id":"gap","kind":"gap","phase":"换情境运用","title":"把表达放回句子","text":"___ your cousins friendly?","options":["Is","Am","Are"],"answer":2,"why":"cousins 是复数，疑问句用 Are。"},{"id":"transfer","kind":"transfer",)NATIVE_DATA";
