static const char chunk40[]=R"NATIVE_DATA(s homework by email. The three friends have different study times, but they all want to understand people more easily.","q":"Mei 和 Ben 的英语课是什么时候？","options":["周二上午七点","周二晚上七点","周六上午九点"],"answer":1,"why":"Tuesday evenings 与 starts at seven 合起来表示周二晚七点；不是另一位人物的课。"},{"id":"read1","kind":"read","phase":"阅读理解","title":"读懂这段信息","text":"Mei and Ben study English together on Tuesday evenings. Their class starts at seven. The teacher gives them a short listening lesson and some homework. Mei works during the day, so she studies at night. She listens to English in the morning on her way to work and reads her notes in the afternoon. Her favourite subject is language. Ben works full-time. He does not study late every night. He does ten minutes of listening practice after work. At the weekend, he takes an online course about computers. Sam works on Tuesday evenings, so he is in a different English class on Saturday mornings. He gets his homework by email. The three friends have different study times, but they all want to understand people more easily.","q":"Ben 每晚都学习到很晚吗？","options":["是，他每晚都学到很晚","没有提到","不是，文中明确否定"],"answer":2,"why":"does not study late every night 是否定，不应只抓住 late 和 every night。"},{"id":"read2","kind":"read","phase":"阅读理解","title":"读懂这段信息","text":"Mei and Ben study English together on Tuesday evenings. Their class starts at seven. The teacher gives them a short listening lesson and some homework. Mei works during the day, so she studies at night. She listens to English in the morning on her way to work and reads her notes in the afternoon. Her favourite subject is language. Ben works full-time. He does not study late every night. He does ten minutes of listening practice after work. At the weekend, he takes an online course about computers. Sam works on Tuesday evenings, so he is in a different English class on Saturday mornings. He gets his homework by email. The three friends have different study times, but they all want to understand people more easily.","q":"为什么 Sam 参加另一班英语课？","options":["他周二晚上要工作","他不想学英语","他在另一个国家"],"answer":0,"why":"because 的意思由 so 前后关系表达：工作安排决定他选择周六班。"},{"id":"read3","kind":"read","phase":"阅读理解","title":"读懂这段信息","text":"Mei and Ben study English together on Tuesday evenings. Their class starts at seven. The teacher gives them a short listening lesson and some homework. Mei works during the day, so she studies at night. She listens to English in the morning on her way to work and reads her notes in the afternoon. Her favourite subject is language. Ben works full-time. He does not study late every night. He does ten minutes of listening practice after work. At the weekend, he takes an online course about computers. Sam works on Tuesday evenings, so he is in a different English class on Saturday mornings. He gets his homework by email. The three friends have different study times, but they all want to understand people more easily.","q":"关于 Ben 的线上课程，哪一项有依据？","options":["是每天晚上的英语课","周末学习计算机相关内容","只能在医院学习"],"answer":1,"why")NATIVE_DATA";
static const char chunk41[]=R"NATIVE_DATA(:"online course about computers 在 at the weekend；与周二英语 class 区别开。"},{"id":"listen0","kind":"listen","phase":"听力理解","title":"先听，再选择","text":"A: Do you study English in the morning, Mei? B: I listen to it in the morning, but my class is at night. A: On Tuesday? B: Yes, at seven.","q":"Mei 的正式英语课在什么时候？","options":["周二晚七点","每天早上七点","周六下午"],"answer":0,"why":"早上听英语与正式上课不是同一件事；后半段给出课的时间。"},{"id":"listen1","kind":"listen","phase":"听力理解","title":"先听，再选择","text":"A: Does Ben do his homework every night? B: No, he does not. He does it on Wednesday. A: Does he study online too? B: Yes, at the weekend.","q":"哪一项符合 Ben 的学习安排？","options":["每晚做作业","周末不上网学习","周三做作业，周末线上学习"],"answer":2,"why":"分别追踪 homework 与 online study 的时间，注意第一句的否定。"},{"id":"listen2","kind":"listen","phase":"听力理解","title":"先听，再选择","text":"A: Is Sam in your Tuesday class? B: No. He works on Tuesday evenings. His English class is on Saturday morning. A: Do you study the same language? B: Yes, English.","q":"Sam 为什么不参加周二班？","options":["他不学英语","他那个时段要工作","他已经结束所有课程"],"answer":1,"why":"work 是本课复现的前课词，解释了为什么选另一个时间的班。"},{"id":"gap","kind":"gap","phase":"换情境运用","title":"把表达放回句子","text":"___ Ben study online at the weekend? Yes, he does.","options":["Do","Is","Does"],"answer":2,"why":"一般现在时第三人称疑问用 Does＋主语＋动词原形 study；you / they 用 Do。"},{"id":"transfer","kind":"transfer","phase":"换情境运用","title":"换个情境，仍然读得懂","q":"同事说“I work at night, but I study in the afternoon.”，应怎样理解？","options":["晚上学习，下午工作","晚上工作，下午学习","工作和学习都在早上"],"answer":1,"why":"分别找到 work 和 study 后面的时间，不把两个动作的安排混在一起。"}],"u2c":[{"id":"recall0","kind":"meaning","phase":"先回顾","wordId":"u1c-w9","title":"还记得 Could you ...? 吗？","text":"Could you repeat the number, please?","options":["一起","能请您……吗？","国家"],"answer":1,"why":"这里复用前课的“能请您……吗？”。"},{"id":"recall1","kind":"meaning","phase":"先回顾","wordId":"u1c-w6","title":"还记得 repeat 吗？","text":"Could you repeat the number?","options":["重复","居住","国家"],"answer":0,"why":"这里复用前课的“重复”。"},{"id":"pair0","kind":"learn","phase":"认识表达","title":"在句子里认识表达","wordIds":["u2c-w1","u2c-w2"]},{"id":"pair1","kind":"learn","phase":"认识表达","title":"在句子里认识表达","wordIds":["u2c-w3","u2c-w4"]},{"id":"pair2","kind":"learn","phase":"认识表达","title":"在句子里认识表达","wordIds":["u2c-w5","u2c-w6"]},{"id":"pair3","kind":"learn","phase":"认识表达","title":"在句子里认识表达","wordIds":["u2c-w7","u2c-w8"]},{"id":"pair4","kind":"learn","phase":"认识表达","title":"在句子里认识表达","wordIds":["u2c-w9"]},{"id":"word0","kind":"meaning","phase":"理解词义","wordId":"u2c-w1","title":"Can I have ...? 在这里是什么意思？","text":"Can I have a pen, please?","options":["可以给我……吗？（索取物品）","认识；见面","名"],"answer":0,"why":"Can I have ...? 在这里表示“可以给我……吗？（索取物品）”。"},{"id":"word1","kind":"meaning","phase":"理解词义","wordId":"u2c-w2","title":"Here you are. 在这里是什么意思？","text":"Here you are. This pen is for you.","options":["无线的","语言","给你。（递交东西时）"],"answer":2,"why":"Here you are. 在这里表示“给你。（递交东西时）”。"},{"id":"word2","kind":"meaning","phase":"理解词义","wordId":"u2c-w3","title":"Anything else? 在这里是什么意思？","text":"Anything else? A)NATIVE_DATA";
static const char chunk42[]=R"NATIVE_DATA( coffee for Ben?","options":["在下午","体贴的；善良的","还需要别的吗？"],"answer":2,"why":"Anything else? 在这里表示“还需要别的吗？”。"},{"id":"word3","kind":"meaning","phase":"理解词义","wordId":"u2c-w4","title":"That’s all, thanks. 在这里是什么意思？","text":"That’s all, thanks. We do not need anything else.","options":["在周末（英式常用搭配）","图书管理员","就这些，谢谢。"],"answer":2,"why":"That’s all, thanks. 在这里表示“就这些，谢谢。”。"},{"id":"word4","kind":"meaning","phase":"理解词义","wordId":"u2c-w5","title":"sorry 在这里是什么意思？","text":"Sorry, could you repeat that, please?","options":["对不起；不好意思（本课用于礼貌请求）","可选择的；选填的","已婚的"],"answer":0,"why":"sorry 在这里表示“对不起；不好意思（本课用于礼貌请求）”。"},{"id":"word5","kind":"meaning","phase":"理解词义","wordId":"u2c-w6","title":"please 在这里是什么意思？","text":"Can I have water, please?","options":["请（礼貌用语）","屏幕","地址"],"answer":0,"why":"please 在这里表示“请（礼貌用语）”。"},{"id":"word6","kind":"meaning","phase":"理解词义","wordId":"u2c-w7","title":"pen 在这里是什么意思？","text":"Can I have a pen for the form?","options":["法国的；法国人","必需的；必填的","钢笔；笔"],"answer":2,"why":"pen 在这里表示“钢笔；笔”。"},{"id":"word7","kind":"meaning","phase":"理解词义","wordId":"u2c-w8","title":"water 在这里是什么意思？","text":"Water is fine, thank you.","options":["水","一门课程；一系列课程","表格；表单"],"answer":0,"why":"water 在这里表示“水”。"},{"id":"word8","kind":"meaning","phase":"理解词义","wordId":"u2c-w9","title":"coffee 在这里是什么意思？","text":"Can I have a coffee for Ben?","options":["咖啡","接待员","当地的"],"answer":0,"why":"coffee 在这里表示“咖啡”。"},{"id":"read0","kind":"read","phase":"阅读理解","title":"读懂这段信息","text":"Before her English class, Mei goes to the reception desk. She says to the receptionist, “Can I have a pen, please?” The receptionist gives her one and says, “Here you are.” Mei says, “Thank you.” Later, Ben and Mei visit Rosa’s café. Ben asks for a coffee and Mei asks for water. Rosa asks, “Anything else?” They reply, “That’s all, thanks.” If you do not hear a request clearly, say, “Sorry, could you repeat that, please?” Sorry can introduce a polite request to hear something again; it does not always mean that you have done something wrong. A request is not the same as confirmation that an item is available.","q":"Mei 在接待处要什么？","options":["咖啡","水","一支笔"],"answer":2,"why":"先区分接待处与咖啡店两个场景；pen 是上课前索取的物品。"},{"id":"read1","kind":"read","phase":"阅读理解","title":"读懂这段信息","text":"Before her English class, Mei goes to the reception desk. She says to the receptionist, “Can I have a pen, please?” The receptionist gives her one and says, “Here you are.” Mei says, “Thank you.” Later, Ben and Mei visit Rosa’s café. Ben asks for a coffee and Mei asks for water. Rosa asks, “Anything else?” They reply, “That’s all, thanks.” If you do not hear a request clearly, say, “Sorry, could you repeat that, please?” Sorry can introduce a polite request to hear something again; it does not always mean that you have done something wrong. A request is not the same as confirmation that an item is available.","q":"“Here you are.” 在这里是什么意思？","options":["给你（递交物品）","你住在哪里","请重复一遍"],"answer":0,"why":"这句话跟随递笔动作，不是询问位置。"},{"id":"read2","k)NATIVE_DATA";
static const char chunk43[]=R"NATIVE_DATA(ind":"read","phase":"阅读理解","title":"读懂这段信息","text":"Before her English class, Mei goes to the reception desk. She says to the receptionist, “Can I have a pen, please?” The receptionist gives her one and says, “Here you are.” Mei says, “Thank you.” Later, Ben and Mei visit Rosa’s café. Ben asks for a coffee and Mei asks for water. Rosa asks, “Anything else?” They reply, “That’s all, thanks.” If you do not hear a request clearly, say, “Sorry, could you repeat that, please?” Sorry can introduce a polite request to hear something again; it does not always mean that you have done something wrong. A request is not the same as confirmation that an item is available.","q":"“That’s all, thanks.” 表明什么？","options":["需要更多咖啡","不再加要其他东西","没听清楚"],"answer":1,"why":"对 Anything else? 的回应，表明请求已经结束。"},{"id":"listen0","kind":"listen","phase":"听力理解","title":"先听，再选择","text":"A: Can I have a pen, please? B: Here you are. A: Thank you. B: Anything else? A: No, that is all, thanks.","q":"对方最后还需要其他物品吗？","options":["需要一杯水","没有其他需要","需要另一支笔"],"answer":1,"why":"听到 Anything else? 后还要继续听回应；that is all 表示没有其他需要。"},{"id":"listen1","kind":"listen","phase":"听力理解","title":"先听，再选择","text":"A: Can I have a coffee, please? B: Sorry, we do not have coffee now. We have water. A: Water is fine, thank you. B: Here you are.","q":"说话者最终拿到什么？","options":["水","咖啡","两种都有"],"answer":0,"why":"最初想要 coffee，但咖啡没有；最终接受并拿到 water。"},{"id":"listen2","kind":"listen","phase":"听力理解","title":"先听，再选择","text":"A: Can I have a pen, please? B: Sorry, could you repeat that? A: A pen, please. B: Of course. Here you are.","q":"为什么对方请求重复？","options":["要更换姓名","在拒绝任何帮助","第一次没听清索取的东西"],"answer":2,"why":"Could you repeat that? 承接第一单元的核对用语；不是拒绝。"},{"id":"listen3","kind":"listen","phase":"听力理解","title":"先听，再选择","text":"A: Can I have water, please? B: Yes. Anything else? A: Can I have a coffee for Ben too? B: Of course. A: Thank you. That is all.","q":"最终一共要哪些饮品？","options":["只有水","只有咖啡","水和给 Ben 的咖啡"],"answer":2,"why":"Anything else? 后新增了 for Ben 的咖啡，要综合整段请求。"},{"id":"gap","kind":"gap","phase":"换情境运用","title":"把表达放回句子","text":"A: Can I have a pen, please? B: ___.","options":["Here you are","I am from Bristol","At the weekend"],"answer":0,"why":"递交物品时用 Here you are；其他两项分别说明来源和时间。"},{"id":"transfer","kind":"transfer","phase":"换情境运用","title":"换个情境，仍然读得懂","q":"同事说“Sorry, could you repeat that, please?”，下一步最合适的是？","options":["结束谈话，不再回应","把刚才的话再说一次","直接登记为拒绝"],"answer":1,"why":"这里 sorry 引出礼貌的重复请求，不能机械理解为道歉或拒绝。"}],"u2d":[{"id":"recall0","kind":"meaning","phase":"先回顾","wordId":"u1c-w1","title":"还记得 first name 吗？","text":"My first name is Alex.","options":["国籍","连接","名"],"answer":2,"why":"这里复用前课的“名”。"},{"id":"recall1","kind":"meaning","phase":"先回顾","wordId":"u1c-w2","title":"还记得 surname 吗？","text":"Could you spell your surname?","options":["更新","屏幕","姓"],"answer":2,"why":"这里复用前课的“姓”。"},{"id":"pair0","kind":"learn","phase":"认识表达","title":"在句子里认识表达","wordIds":["u2d-w1","u2d-w2"]},{"id":"pair1","kind":"learn","phase":"认识表达","title":)NATIVE_DATA";
static const char chunk44[]=R"NATIVE_DATA("在句子里认识表达","wordIds":["u2d-w3","u2d-w4"]},{"id":"pair2","kind":"learn","phase":"认识表达","title":"在句子里认识表达","wordIds":["u2d-w5","u2d-w6"]},{"id":"word0","kind":"meaning","phase":"理解词义","wordId":"u2d-w1","title":"form 在这里是什么意思？","text":"Please check the name on this form.","options":["设备","表格；表单","就这些，谢谢。"],"answer":1,"why":"form 在这里表示“表格；表单”。"},{"id":"word1","kind":"meaning","phase":"理解词义","wordId":"u2d-w2","title":"required 在这里是什么意思？","text":"Your email is required on this form.","options":["经理；管理者","必需的；必填的","居住"],"answer":1,"why":"required 在这里表示“必需的；必填的”。"},{"id":"word2","kind":"meaning","phase":"理解词义","wordId":"u2d-w3","title":"optional 在这里是什么意思？","text":"Your phone number is optional.","options":["能请您……吗？","可选择的；选填的","是……对吗？（核对信息）"],"answer":1,"why":"optional 在这里表示“可选择的；选填的”。"},{"id":"word3","kind":"meaning","phase":"理解词义","wordId":"u2d-w4","title":"date of birth 在这里是什么意思？","text":"The date of birth box is optional on this form.","options":["学科；科目","出生日期","兼职的；兼职地"],"answer":1,"why":"date of birth 在这里表示“出生日期”。"},{"id":"word4","kind":"meaning","phase":"理解词义","wordId":"u2d-w5","title":"phone number 在这里是什么意思？","text":"Please check your phone number.","options":["电话号码","公司","忙碌的"],"answer":0,"why":"phone number 在这里表示“电话号码”。"},{"id":"word5","kind":"meaning","phase":"理解词义","wordId":"u2d-w6","title":"signature 在这里是什么意思？","text":"Ben adds his signature to the form.","options":["可选择的；选填的","就这些，谢谢。","签名"],"answer":2,"why":"signature 在这里表示“签名”。"},{"id":"read0","kind":"read","phase":"阅读理解","title":"读懂这段信息","text":"Bristol English Centre. Course registration form. Please use capital letters for your name. First name: BEN. Surname: CARTER. Job: engineer. Course: English after work. Class: Tuesday at 7 p.m. Required information: first name, surname, email and signature. Optional information: phone number and date of birth. Ben uses ben.carter@example.com as his email. He leaves the optional phone number box empty. The centre uses email to contact him about the course. Check your name and class before you sign. Ben asks for a pen and adds his signature. A second page asks for an address and postcode only if you want a letter by post. Ben chooses email, so he does not complete that page. Required means you must provide the information on this form; optional means you can choose whether to provide it.","q":"这张报名表中哪一项是必填？","options":["出生日期","签名","电话号码"],"answer":1,"why":"Required information 中有 signature；另外两项位于 Optional information。此规则只针对这张示例表。"},{"id":"read1","kind":"read","phase":"阅读理解","title":"读懂这段信息","text":"Bristol English Centre. Course registration form. Please use capital letters for your name. First name: BEN. Surname: CARTER. Job: engineer. Course: English after work. Class: Tuesday at 7 p.m. Required information: first name, surname, email and signature. Optional information: phone number and date of birth. Ben uses ben.carter@example.com as his email. He leaves the optional phone number box empty. The centre uses email to contact him about the course)NATIVE_DATA";
