static const char chunk65[]=R"NATIVE_DATA(09ce328a3.wav","course":"audio/a200eecf07c0f182c255.wav","Ben takes an online course about computers.":"audio/68773a39b030045d91bb.wav","class":"audio/d37f2157d91786cd00a1.wav","Our English class starts at seven.":"audio/86de4a1e85edfd144161.wav","lesson":"audio/046efcb3ded7e2f1acd0.wav","This listening lesson is short.":"audio/0720e65f869a41e6d6b3.wav","practice":"audio/98935264d48df51cca41.wav","Ben does listening practice after work.":"audio/227c542c6b87751d59b0.wav","homework":"audio/56ee90328de5d768a4d4.wav","The teacher sends homework by email.":"audio/19340ef6555e35440de0.wav","subject":"audio/4344ddef83b369f1a846.wav","What is your favourite subject?":"audio/463b03943683c3799a5b.wav","online":"audio/51359cee1dded4a2fb9f.wav","Ben studies online at the weekend.":"audio/01037814ce893224ab85.wav","at night":"audio/4624e43b2fa5edaf8202.wav","Mei studies at night.":"audio/288eb59b969ade1da143.wav","in the morning":"audio/afc71bc3eb4103f9b678.wav","I listen to English in the morning.":"audio/60b6da9c85ad638016be.wav","in the afternoon":"audio/0025a81db2f9d49d3f80.wav","She reads her notes in the afternoon.":"audio/7fab4edabc7067b09f19.wav","at the weekend":"audio/a45afeb33ab478c592e9.wav","Ben takes an online course at the weekend.":"audio/28471a252bd949d707f5.wav","Can I have ...?":"audio/fecdfcbb822149c2057f.wav","Can I have a pen, please?":"audio/dc11236f16cc93412e22.wav","Here you are.":"audio/3728ea426539aa11908d.wav","Here you are. This pen is for you.":"audio/91cd5e6eac22d66d171a.wav","Anything else?":"audio/f2eca87f87c4ba050e37.wav","Anything else? A coffee for Ben?":"audio/fb3a898923fbd7be894e.wav","That’s all, thanks.":"audio/a0a59dfda3399ac79fed.wav","That’s all, thanks. We do not need anything else.":"audio/86235d2c53a265209fa3.wav","sorry":"audio/a4f7f9dc31ef2a634a74.wav","Sorry, could you repeat that, please?":"audio/07787d7fe6619ba571a8.wav","please":"audio/4cdc7b2550ce3059549f.wav","Can I have water, please?":"audio/edd9615013d6b2e304cb.wav","pen":"audio/9fa9c6173e1beaff9ed0.wav","Can I have a pen for the form?":"audio/abbe167d762329173269.wav","water":"audio/f0e0c6091918b8cacbb9.wav","Water is fine, thank you.":"audio/d36ab5a1a58ac04632f5.wav","coffee":"audio/a670e2f6a4de7a41a64b.wav","Can I have a coffee for Ben?":"audio/f517419504198ee7fc56.wav","form":"audio/bac759a79cfb80388b61.wav","Please check the name on this form.":"audio/a2d2e1f98965fd3f6a30.wav","required":"audio/e60faeebb1fcaa4cee3b.wav","Your email is required on this form.":"audio/9c0e48246a5353e04417.wav","optional":"audio/d2ad54a790fbb9a3fbc5.wav","Your phone number is optional.":"audio/ecc4025f0fbf5c08f97e.wav","date of birth":"audio/f086a1577d5b0fd94b5b.wav","The date of birth box is optional on this form.":"audio/1b762211101667340339.wav","phone number":"audio/215fe4677b38c040895a.wav","Please check your phone number.":"audio/e0e992aeca64414a7256.wav","signature":"audio/67c00eb98282a50529b6.wav","Ben adds his signature to the form.":"audio/8580b0b1cff7d2c8695)NATIVE_DATA";
static const char chunk66[]=R"NATIVE_DATA(b.wav","capital letters":"audio/6c73c321917a2677a5e0.wav","Please use capital letters.":"audio/e0fa55dcb6e33eda65a3.wav","postcode":"audio/9a3ed17f9cddc40f26ca.wav","Add a postcode if you choose a letter by post.":"audio/c7a86eec6a5391b33d96.wav","I am Mei. I am from China, but I live in Bristol now. Ben is my colleague. He is Canadian and lives near our office. Our neighbour Rosa is from Brazil. Anna is French, but her home is in Bristol too. Tom is British. His colleague Max is German. On a registration form, nationality means the country you belong to. It does not always tell people where you live now. We often meet at a small café after work.":"audio/968e0ef7df6ddc5cca28.wav","A: Hi, I am Sam. Are you from Canada? B: No, I am from Australia. I live in Leeds now. A: Nice to meet you.":"audio/6297667fbe2ecfc62818.wav","A: Is Rosa your colleague? B: No, she is my neighbour. My colleague is Ben. He is Canadian.":"audio/74190c21efe44635044a.wav","A: Are Anna and Max British? B: No. Anna is French, and Max is German. They both live in Bristol. A: So Bristol is their home now? B: Yes.":"audio/bb3735e20f5dbb3496ef.wav","Ben is Mei’s colleague. He is usually quiet at work, but he is friendly and helpful. He helps new colleagues find the right room. His cousin Leo is tall and likes talking to people. Leo is married. Ben is single and lives with a friend. Their neighbour Rosa works in a busy café. She is kind to the people who visit. Ben and Rosa study English together on Tuesday evenings. A quiet person can still be friendly; one adjective does not tell you everything about a person.":"audio/420963586ba0916ba0c3.wav","A: Is your new colleague friendly? B: Yes, and she is very helpful. A: Is she quiet? B: Not really. She likes talking to people.":"audio/4b8604fd15e7ed567145.wav","A: Are you busy on Tuesday evening? B: Yes. My cousin and I study English together. I am free on Wednesday.":"audio/40ea8189f28b1ac495b0.wav","A friendly receptionist helps you join the English group. First name: Alex. Surname: Park. City: Bristol. Country: the United Kingdom. Home address: 18 King Street. Email: alex.park@example.com. Please check your first name, surname and address before you send the form. If a number is not correct, ask the receptionist to change it. You can say, “Could you repeat the number, please?” Then check it: “Is that eighteen King Street?” Do not guess a number that you have not heard clearly.":"audio/66092bbadceb04b3213d.wav","A: What is your surname? B: Park. A: Could you spell that, please? B: P, A, R, K. A: Thank you.":"audio/c99f0446c48f6a88bfdf.wav","A: Is your address thirteen King Street? B: No, eighteen King Street. A: Eighteen? B: Yes, that is correct.":"audio/f0814e8500633c0561a8.wav","A: Is your first name Park? B: No. Alex is my first name. Park is my surname. A: Alex Park? B: That is right.":"audio/0005f9b87e62dcb18b35.wav","A: Could you repeat your city, please? B: Bristol. A: Is that in Canada? B: No. Bristol is in the United Kingdo)NATIVE_DATA";
static const char chunk67[]=R"NATIVE_DATA(m. I am Canadian, but I live here now.":"audio/be1a9cbc5523fc18be48.wav","Hello, I am Mei. I am from China and live in Bristol. I work at a local library. My interests are music and walking. I study English in the evening because I want to meet people in my city. You can contact me by email about our English group. My profile shows my first name, city and interests. It does not show my home address or private phone number. Ben’s profile says he is Canadian and works near my library. He is friendly and helpful. His interests are films and music. Our profiles give useful information, but they do not tell readers everything about us.":"audio/3e9defea7d87ce424837.wav","A: How can I contact you about the English group, Mei? B: Please send me an email. My home address is not on my profile. A: That is fine. I only need the group information.":"audio/73979fcb84ee941d0bdf.wav","A: Your profile says you work in a shop. Is that correct? B: No. That is my old job. I work in a library now. A: Could you update the profile? B: Yes, thank you.":"audio/4493f1ca44868c6a2ada.wav","The office has got a new wireless screen. You can connect your device without a cable. First, join the office network. Then open the screen app. You need an account, but the app does not need permission to read your contacts. Save your work before you install an update.":"audio/2af8349e707df7e1a0e4.wav","A: Have you got a cable for this screen? B: We do not need one. It is wireless. Join the office network first, then open the app.":"audio/77def43eabfe285a6dea.wav","A: The app asks for permission to use the microphone. Do I need to allow it? B: Only for a voice call. You can read messages without it.":"audio/84c89184235db5ec5f0e.wav","New members of the English group. Noor is from Egypt and lives in Bristol. She works at a local library. Her interests are music and films. Ben is Canadian. He lives in Bristol too. He is quiet but friendly, and he studies English on Tuesday evenings. To contact the group, send an email to the receptionist. Members do not have to share their home addresses on their profiles.":"audio/42e37ab6bdc326a57b5d.wav","Reception note. First name: Alex. Surname: Park. City: Bristol. Address: 18 King Street. Please check these details. If a name or number is wrong, ask the receptionist to repeat it. A form can contain an old job or a spelling mistake, so read the information carefully before you confirm it.":"audio/832d93ba7766ff40509a.wav","A: Is Noor your colleague? B: No, she is my neighbour. We both work in libraries, but we work in different places.":"audio/f6c484ec80eff95eae8c.wav","A: Are you British, Ben? B: No, I am Canadian. I live in Bristol now. A: So your home is in Britain? B: Yes, that is right.":"audio/464c4030930184751179.wav","A: Your address is thirteen King Street. B: Could you repeat the number, please? A: Thirteen. B: That is not correct. It is eighteen. A: Eighteen King Street. B: That is right.":"audio/37031b9cb96975ad34b3.wav","A: Is Leo single?)NATIVE_DATA";
static const char chunk68[]=R"NATIVE_DATA( B: No, he is married. His cousin Ben is single. They are both in the English group. Leo comes on Wednesday and Ben comes on Tuesday.":"audio/3ca3ef7bbfc9925140fc.wav","Mei works at a local library in Bristol. She is a librarian. Her colleague Ben is friendly and helpful. He is an engineer at a small software company. He works with Mei on the library’s software. He works in an office, not in a hospital. Ben works full-time. His cousin Leo is a manager at a shop. Leo works part-time because he also studies. Their neighbour Rosa works in a café. Her friend Sam is a waiter there. Maya is a nurse at the local hospital; her brother is a doctor. Eva is a teacher and teaches adults. Arun is a driver. He takes people to work. At the English centre, a receptionist answers questions about classes. A job title tells you what someone does, but it does not always tell you where or how many hours they work.":"audio/b37b97bc5c24d58f5b4b.wav","A: What does Ben do? B: He is an engineer. A: Does he work in a hospital? B: No, he works in an office at a software company.":"audio/aff9279e698cf601dddb.wav","A: Is Leo a driver? B: No, he is a manager in a shop. A: Does he work full-time? B: No, he works part-time. He studies too.":"audio/18ab167f54d48be52639.wav","A: I work at the local hospital. B: Are you a doctor, Maya? A: No, I am a nurse. My brother is a doctor.":"audio/179f7b19ce89d935c44f.wav","Mei and Ben study English together on Tuesday evenings. Their class starts at seven. The teacher gives them a short listening lesson and some homework. Mei works during the day, so she studies at night. She listens to English in the morning on her way to work and reads her notes in the afternoon. Her favourite subject is language. Ben works full-time. He does not study late every night. He does ten minutes of listening practice after work. At the weekend, he takes an online course about computers. Sam works on Tuesday evenings, so he is in a different English class on Saturday mornings. He gets his homework by email. The three friends have different study times, but they all want to understand people more easily.":"audio/6b983527abc411f9ff91.wav","A: Do you study English in the morning, Mei? B: I listen to it in the morning, but my class is at night. A: On Tuesday? B: Yes, at seven.":"audio/670e7c8e8fd22fbd52d9.wav","A: Does Ben do his homework every night? B: No, he does not. He does it on Wednesday. A: Does he study online too? B: Yes, at the weekend.":"audio/19553c0cf923d0d8a83e.wav","A: Is Sam in your Tuesday class? B: No. He works on Tuesday evenings. His English class is on Saturday morning. A: Do you study the same language? B: Yes, English.":"audio/cff41f06ffc2f9796490.wav","Before her English class, Mei goes to the reception desk. She says to the receptionist, “Can I have a pen, please?” The receptionist gives her one and says, “Here you are.” Mei says, “Thank you.” Later, Ben and Mei visit Rosa’s café. Ben asks for a coffee and Mei asks for water. Rosa asks, “An)NATIVE_DATA";
static const char chunk69[]=R"NATIVE_DATA(ything else?” They reply, “That’s all, thanks.” If you do not hear a request clearly, say, “Sorry, could you repeat that, please?” Sorry can introduce a polite request to hear something again; it does not always mean that you have done something wrong. A request is not the same as confirmation that an item is available.":"audio/881356c8c2d343f8ee7e.wav","A: Can I have a pen, please? B: Here you are. A: Thank you. B: Anything else? A: No, that is all, thanks.":"audio/49c7f985013f998975b5.wav","A: Can I have a coffee, please? B: Sorry, we do not have coffee now. We have water. A: Water is fine, thank you. B: Here you are.":"audio/46c030398e0d391f53d9.wav","A: Can I have a pen, please? B: Sorry, could you repeat that? A: A pen, please. B: Of course. Here you are.":"audio/b575c66e7104a62722b5.wav","A: Can I have water, please? B: Yes. Anything else? A: Can I have a coffee for Ben too? B: Of course. A: Thank you. That is all.":"audio/0b2495cc222c8e64bbee.wav","Bristol English Centre. Course registration form. Please use capital letters for your name. First name: BEN. Surname: CARTER. Job: engineer. Course: English after work. Class: Tuesday at 7 p.m. Required information: first name, surname, email and signature. Optional information: phone number and date of birth. Ben uses ben.carter@example.com as his email. He leaves the optional phone number box empty. The centre uses email to contact him about the course. Check your name and class before you sign. Ben asks for a pen and adds his signature. A second page asks for an address and postcode only if you want a letter by post. Ben chooses email, so he does not complete that page. Required means you must provide the information on this form; optional means you can choose whether to provide it.":"audio/79735810b1bfb844b8a5.wav","A: Do I need to write my phone number? B: No, that is optional on this form. Your email is required. A: Fine. Please contact me by email.":"audio/8fcaccf504a66e5b8b0a.wav","A: Your class is on Thursday at seven, Ben. B: Sorry, that is not correct. My class is on Tuesday at seven in the evening. A: Tuesday at seven in the evening. Is that right? B: Yes, thank you.":"audio/27ef0f606ffaa66fd2b7.wav","A: Can I have a pen, please? I need to add my signature. B: Here you are. A: Do I need to add my date of birth too? B: No, that is optional.":"audio/5de4018f3239bb17735f.wav","New members at Bristol English Centre. Sara is from Canada and lives in Bristol. She is a nurse at a hospital. She works part-time and studies English on Monday evenings. Her colleague Omar is a doctor. He works full-time and takes an online course at the weekend. Their neighbour Dan is a driver. He is quiet but helpful. He listens to English in the morning and does his homework in the afternoon. Sara and Dan are in the same English class. Omar is in a different class. They all use email to contact the centre.":"audio/62d504ec3b7fa1b5ce58.wav","A note for new students. Before class, ask the receptionist if you nee)NATIVE_DATA";
static const char chunk70[]=R"NATIVE_DATA(d a pen. Say, “Can I have a pen, please?” If you do not hear the reply, ask the person to repeat it. At the café you can ask for coffee or water. When the waiter asks, “Anything else?”, say, “That’s all, thanks” if you do not want more. Always listen to the final reply: a requested item may not be available.":"audio/45bc76abf111c6f0110c.wav","Evening course form. First name: Sara. Surname: Ali. Job: nurse. Class: Monday at 6 p.m. Required: first name, surname, email, signature. Optional: phone number, date of birth. Contact: sara.ali@example.com. Sara chooses email and leaves the optional phone number empty. Please check all required information before you sign. This form does not ask for a home address.":"audio/0c3526f9731e85b76a92.wav","A: Are you a doctor, Sara? B: No, I am a nurse. Omar is a doctor. A: Does he work part-time? B: No. He works full-time. I work part-time.":"audio/2673caa83a1050f19885.wav","A: Do you study in the morning, Dan? B: I listen to English then. I do my homework in the afternoon. A: Is your class on Monday evening? B: Yes, with Sara.":"audio/a96dc030c9aa075baebb.wav","A: Can I have a coffee, please? B: Sorry, we do not have coffee today. A: Water is fine. B: Here you are. Anything else? A: No, that is all, thanks.":"audio/173e34d89011be418907.wav","A: Is your class on Tuesday at six, Sara? B: No, Monday at six in the evening. A: Monday at six. Is that correct? B: Yes. A: Please add your signature. Your phone number is optional.":"audio/3fb58060336e35eac835.wav","I am Mei. I am from China, but I live in Bristol now. My colleague Ben is Canadian. He lives near the office. Our neighbour Rosa is from Brazil. We often meet at a small café after work.":"audio/648c603b1020402c2878.wav","Leo is my cousin. He is tall and usually quiet, but he is very friendly when you know him. He works in a busy café. His colleague Nora is helpful. They study English together on Tuesday evenings.":"audio/cb8ca28d9ec24c0ae0d3.wav","Registration note: First name: Alex. Surname: Park. Address: 18 King Street. Please check your name and address before you send the form. If a number is not correct, ask the receptionist to change it.":"audio/dfe5fe8375ac66a3725f.wav","Hello, I am Lina. I work at a local library and study English in the evening. My interests are music and walking. This public profile shows my first name and interests. It does not show my home address or private phone number. Please contact me by email.":"audio/19c59d2f7e51ea23d9ca.wav","A: How can I contact you about the English group? B: Please send me an email. My private phone number is not on my profile.":"audio/29f731192e68d9b113d3.wav","A: Does your profile say you work in a shop? B: No. That is my old job. I work in a library now.":"audio/8076264f40712dbf9a04.wav","This is a sound check. You do not need to answer a question. Please adjust the volume until you can hear this sentence clearly.":"audio/8d14ee5ed3d87bcea932.wav","A: Where is the bus stop? B: It is next to the stati)NATIVE_DATA";
static const char chunk71[]=R"NATIVE_DATA(on, not the bank. A: Thank you.":"audio/ce2b3864633544d21dc7.wav","A: Is the appointment on Wednesday at three? B: No, Thursday at three in the afternoon. A: Thursday afternoon? B: Yes.":"audio/7ce3e19b1c0600c364ce.wav","A: Can I use the printer now? B: It is offline today. Please email me the file for now. We can print it tomorrow.":"audio/6dc6e8a1483a0e6d5ade.wav","A: Have you installed the update? B: I have downloaded it, but I have not installed it yet. I will wait until the meeting finishes.":"audio/02c47f84de285dff21bf.wav","A: Would you like tea or coffee? B: Tea, please. No sugar.":"audio/0e7f65b7c09aea10b90e.wav","A: What time is lunch? B: At twelve. A: Thank you.":"audio/bd10c879f80d81b54f68.wav","A: Is this your bag? B: No, my bag is blue. This one is red.":"audio/665236ec6fa485632477.wav","A: Is the screen on? B: Yes, but there is no picture.":"audio/b8409aae34d62d63addc.wav","A: Which button? B: The small one on the left.":"audio/65f9ee8bc5a5cbd88ba8.wav","A: Where is the cable? B: In the box next to the computer.":"audio/c12f6b4a074aec788482.wav","A: Can we meet at ten? B: I have a call then. How about half past ten? A: That works.":"audio/5a6a4d26e431333ffe94.wav","A: A room for two nights? B: Actually, three. I will leave on Friday. A: I will change the booking.":"audio/30f7a3827e8f8f5b56d1.wav","A: Can I pay by card? B: Usually yes, but the machine is not working today. Cash only, I am afraid.":"audio/c7167e23ccfb150599c3.wav","A: Do I restart now? B: Save your work first. Then close the app and restart the computer.":"audio/b7c46fc69f3cc4b605ef.wav","A: The message says the password is wrong. B: Check the capital letters before you reset it.":"audio/18cd941f2a9337d21fef.wav","A: Did you send the report? B: I saved it, but I have not uploaded it yet. I will do that after lunch.":"audio/7b6dc5bd281a8529ccab.wav","A: Shall we book the cheaper flight? B: It lands after the last train. A: A taxi would cost more than the difference. B: Then let us take the earlier flight.":"audio/195da539e15c1965286c.wav","A: Can you cover my shift on Monday? B: Only if I can leave by four. A: That is fine; I will be back by then.":"audio/226d64c96a59a2b262b8.wav","A: The venue is available on both dates. B: The speakers can only come on the later one. A: Let us confirm that date before paying the deposit.":"audio/1f793b79acb483da9b33.wav","A: The download has finished. Shall I install it? B: Not until we copy the current settings. A: Even with a backup? B: Yes, keep a separate copy for this change.":"audio/2521586400f78a538e6a.wav","A: The test failed only when two clients connected at once. B: So a single-user test would miss it. A: Exactly. Let us add a concurrent test before release.":"audio/deeb88a1aa11c39ea237.wav","A: Is the data gone? B: The files are still there; the index is damaged. A: Can we rebuild it? B: Yes, after we copy the files to a safe location.":"audio/7a0ff875c60ecae39fc7.wav","A: The consultation attracted many comments. B: Yes)NATIVE_DATA";
static const char chunk72[]=R"NATIVE_DATA(, though we cannot infer how common each view is; people with strong opinions were more likely to respond. A: So we should use it to identify concerns, not estimate public support.":"audio/461a236e5733dc2af3e6.wav","A: Could we promise delivery by Friday? B: Only provisionally. The component is due tomorrow, but customs clearance remains uncertain. A: Then let us offer an estimate and explain the dependency.":"audio/ade48a1a9359f8fcb825.wav","A: The pilot saved time. B: For experienced staff, yes. New starters needed extra guidance. A: Then the overall figure hides an important difference. B: We should report the groups separately.":"audio/8f785f9ebf1561143478.wav","A: The new model uses less memory. B: But it repeats part of the computation for every chunk. A: So the smaller footprint does not guarantee lower latency. B: We need measurements on the target device.":"audio/599d7ccbb311b61e64b5.wav","A: The encrypted channel passed inspection. B: That says little about the logs at the endpoint. A: Agreed. Credentials might still be written there. B: Let us audit logging before declaring the system secure.":"audio/2de45e84ffe83e538e2c.wav","A: Average throughput increased, but the slowest requests got worse. B: Then a blanket improvement claim would be misleading. A: We should state the trade-off and include tail latency.":"audio/cc41cd852c3dbf3fc243.wav","Our walking tour was planned for Saturday, but heavy rain is expected. The organiser offers two alternatives: postpone the tour until Sunday or take an indoor city visit on Saturday. The Sunday tour costs the same, and the deposit can be transferred. The indoor visit costs less, so the difference will be refunded. Confirm your choice by Thursday evening. If neither option meets your requirements, you can request a full refund before Friday.":"audio/6fcdcc8a21b7178a5782.wav","postpone":"audio/52f01c8784fdab4c04c7.wav","We may need to postpone the visit.":"audio/aa7621657e58719ed7f2.wav","alternative":"audio/d2a8f3b668e571f87bc3.wav","The train is a useful alternative.":"audio/2d369b0c82613e53108e.wav","confirm":"audio/61fa9ef9f7e1773caf1e.wav","Please confirm the time by tomorrow.":"audio/1ae6631b0003af482999.wav","deposit":"audio/9ca767cd5c05715aef56.wav","We have not paid the deposit yet.":"audio/0782face3b4ff5b2347a.wav","refund":"audio/1ab00c689e43b9b80d63.wav","You can request a refund before Friday.":"audio/18603d7432e47328a3c0.wav","requirement":"audio/82d2bc190f73e8825fcf.wav","Check the requirements before booking.":"audio/d17664a870252c0a1380.wav","A: Shall we postpone the visit until Sunday? B: I cannot come then. Is the indoor visit still available on Saturday? A: Yes, and it is cheaper. B: Please confirm that option for me.":"audio/9e6d93142f1fc33cfe61.wav","A: Have you paid the deposit? B: Not yet. I am checking the access requirements first. A: Good idea. Confirm those before you book.":"audio/e479f2948e58a076bd25.wav","Before updating the reporting tool, verify that its dependencies)NATIVE_DATA";
static const char chunk73[]=R"NATIVE_DATA( are compatible with the new version. Copy the current settings and restore a sample from the backup. A backup file alone does not prove that recovery will work. If the update fails, a rollback can restore the previous version and settings. The temporary solution is to keep using the old tool, but record the fault so that the team can reproduce it. Do not delete the old files until the updated tool has passed the agreed checks.":"audio/2905afa94efe9dd8f90a.wav","restore":"audio/21ef74bcb56b6dffe5c0.wav","Restore a sample before relying on the backup.":"audio/612a446889cfed309f03.wav","compatible":"audio/cc432680cf0254643df6.wav","Check that the new version is compatible.":"audio/13b1625b0da610aa1964.wav","temporary":"audio/0c329b7db84864f5f66a.wav","This is a temporary solution.":"audio/f6087e01205f312a20f2.wav","verify":"audio/86faa4c752da02d9a41c.wav","Verify that the copied files can be opened.":"audio/fd59edfc6147bdd9ac55.wav","rollback":"audio/c88e8f6f858b2f53dd95.wav","Keep the old files for a rollback.":"audio/6a2a941fa5397d9988a7.wav","dependency":"audio/278c08576613c900d6c2.wav","One dependency needs an update.":"audio/9b285b342350e368d4ad.wav","A: The new tool starts, but one report is missing. B: Did you verify the restored settings? A: Not yet. B: Check those before changing the data files.":"audio/bc9919622d0d5e8acec1.wav","A: Should we roll back? B: The new version is incompatible with one dependency. A: Then keep the old version for now and record the issue.":"audio/06d326df4247f0efb0fb.wav","The venue has offered a provisional reservation at a reduced price, contingent on confirmation by Tuesday. The discount applies only to groups of at least twenty. Smaller groups remain eligible for the standard package but cannot claim the reduced rate. The main constraint is flexibility: changing the date after confirmation normally incurs a fee. The venue may waive this fee if severe weather prevents travel, provided that supporting evidence is supplied. We should therefore compare the saving with the risk of later changes and agree on a contingency before confirming.":"audio/eccb275bedec2c23ee42.wav","provisional":"audio/211c2aab80fbe72a0be2.wav","The reservation remains provisional.":"audio/0e6c823a2c02810968ed.wav","constraint":"audio/373a03bb4ad4eb3352e9.wav","Explain the main constraint before agreeing.":"audio/f8937cd5aac47f961e1b.wav","contingency":"audio/88ccf53b447d38bfc6ab.wav","We need a contingency for bad weather.":"audio/8c09fc0180193033eb76.wav","eligible":"audio/ea6e5a162fbb71c30d42.wav","Check whether your booking is eligible.":"audio/3cf487690f24f10fd00b.wav","waive":"audio/b97bec080d4d11015935.wav","The hotel may waive the cancellation fee.":"audio/c80771c74b99600c1671.wav","trade-off":"audio/b5c7171717223ad339e3.wav","There is a trade-off between price and flexibility.":"audio/38e9385345a5e5bb1605.wav","A: Can we promise everyone that changes will be free? B: No. The venue may waive the fee, but only with evidence of seve)NATIVE_DATA";
static const char chunk74[]=R"NATIVE_DATA(re weather. A: Then we should explain the condition rather than promise an automatic refund.":"audio/fb1ff136d802a356af8c.wav","A: The reduced rate looks attractive. B: But it removes the option to change dates without a fee. A: Since our schedule is uncertain, flexibility may be worth the extra cost.":"audio/8d1f351cbf37f43e8561.wav","The smaller model reduced memory use but introduced additional setup overhead for each chunk. On the target device, this overhead became the bottleneck. Caching mitigated repeated work, yet it did not reduce the latency of the first request. A second experiment increased throughput by processing requests together, while the longest waits became worse. Neither result supports an unqualified claim that the system is faster. The report should separate first-request latency, cached replay and throughput, using representative workloads and the same output-quality checks for every comparison.":"audio/60b4d19ee85b25a0c241.wav","overhead":"audio/01b54020c7167fdd84c2.wav","Repeated setup adds overhead.":"audio/b9f9843787e2858ad94a.wav","bottleneck":"audio/1400ac2652e06708e3d3.wav","Measure the bottleneck before optimising.":"audio/fee152b5a2049b8d2471.wav","latency":"audio/471ccac77a64b29bd6e6.wav","Lower latency makes the app feel faster.":"audio/865eff59330b99a1dd11.wav","throughput":"audio/f9f954221f4ca28382cc.wav","Higher throughput does not guarantee low latency.":"audio/d63f93676cc641960632.wav","representative":"audio/3418bddc98426f115c0e.wav","Choose a representative workload.":"audio/f18543fedfe1e1051f24.wav","mitigate":"audio/6bd99470d42e525d7657.wav","Caching can mitigate repeated work.":"audio/bd6361e9fcb6c794f7fe.wav","A: The cached replay takes almost no time. B: That does not tell us how long the first request takes. A: Right. We should publish both timings with the same sentence and quality settings.":"audio/b758900807266274f82f.wav","A: Can we fix the bottleneck with more threads? B: Perhaps, but memory access may already be saturated. A: Then measure that before adding concurrency.":"audio/9c5557f9f93370a0aa34.wav"}})NATIVE_DATA";
